<h1>Flavors of the Northeast: A Culinary Journey</h1>

<section class="region-overview mb-2">
    <p>Northeast India offers a unique and tantalizing culinary experience, distinct from the rest of the country. Influenced by its diverse ethnicities, geography, and proximity to Southeast Asia, the cuisine is characterized by simple cooking methods, fresh local ingredients, fermented foods, and often minimal use of oil and spices, letting the natural flavors shine through. From fiery ghost peppers to subtle bamboo shoots, explore the diverse tastes that define this region.</p>
    <p>Here's a taste of some signature dishes and ingredients you might encounter:</p>
</section>

<hr class="mb-2">

<section class="food-showcase">
    <h2>Signature Dishes & Ingredients</h2>

    <div class="tribe-grid">

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/E8E8E8/969696?text=Assam+Laksa+(Tenga)" alt="Representation of Assamese Fish Curry (Masor Tenga)">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Masor Tenga (Assam)</h3>
                <p>A staple in Assamese households, this tangy fish curry gets its sourness from ingredients like tomatoes, ou tenga (elephant apple), or lemon. It's light, flavorful, and perfectly complements steamed rice.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/D0D0D0/969696?text=Smoked+Pork+with+Bamboo+Shoot" alt="Representation of Smoked Pork with Bamboo Shoot">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Smoked Pork with Bamboo Shoot (Nagaland/Mizoram/Arunachal)</h3>
                <p>A beloved dish across several states, featuring chunks of smoked pork cooked with fermented or fresh bamboo shoots. Often flavored with raja mircha (ghost pepper), it offers a smoky, pungent, and spicy kick.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/E8E8E8/969696?text=Iromba+Manipur" alt="Representation of Iromba">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Iromba (Manipur)</h3>
                <p>A quintessential Manipuri side dish or chutney made from mashed boiled vegetables (like potatoes, beans, colocasia), fermented fish (ngari), and fiery chilies. It's known for its strong, pungent aroma and flavor.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/D0D0D0/969696?text=Jadoh+Meghalaya" alt="Representation of Jadoh">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Jadoh (Meghalaya)</h3>
                <p>A popular Khasi delicacy, Jadoh is rice cooked with meat, usually pork (sometimes chicken), often enriched with pork blood (optional). It's subtly flavored with ginger, turmeric, and onions, creating a savory and hearty meal.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/E8E8E8/969696?text=Thukpa+Noodles" alt="Representation of Thukpa">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Thukpa (Sikkim / Arunachal Pradesh)</h3>
                <p>A hearty noodle soup with Tibetan origins, popular in the Himalayan states. It typically contains noodles, vegetables, and meat (like chicken, pork, or yak) in a flavorful broth, perfect for cold weather.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/D0D0D0/969696?text=Apong+Rice+Beer" alt="Representation of Apong / Rice Beer">
            <div class="tribe-card-body">
                <h3>Apong / Zu / Local Rice Beer (Various States)</h3>
                <p>Traditional home-brewed alcoholic beverages made from fermented rice or millet are common across the Northeast. Known by different names (Apong, Zu, Tho, etc.), they play a significant role in social and ritualistic life.</p>
                <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
             <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/E8E8E8/969696?text=Bamboo+Shoot" alt="Representation of Bamboo Shoots in cooking">
             <div class="tribe-card-body">
                 <h3>Bamboo Shoots (Ingredient)</h3>
                 <p>A ubiquitous ingredient used extensively across the region, both fresh and fermented. Bamboo shoots add a unique texture and slightly tangy or pungent flavor to curries, stir-fries, and pickles.</p>
                 <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
             </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tribe-card">
             <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x200/D0D0D0/969696?text=Raja+Mircha" alt="Representation of Raja Mircha / Ghost Pepper">
             <div class="tribe-card-body">
                 <h3>Raja Mircha / Bhut Jolokia (Ingredient)</h3>
                 <p>Famously known as the Ghost Pepper, once the world's hottest chili. Used (sparingly!) in many dishes and pickles across Nagaland, Assam, and Manipur to add intense heat and a unique fruity flavor.</p>
                 <a href="#" class="card-link">Learn More (Soon)</a>
             </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>

